WEBVTT

00:00.610 --> 00:04.360
THEREFORE, IT IS IRREFUTABLE
THAT THE CULPRIT IS...

00:08.609 --> 00:10.240
A security camera?

00:10.240 --> 00:11.990
There definitely wasn't one earlier.

00:11.990 --> 00:13.119
I'm sure of it.

00:21.670 --> 00:24.839
Reality alteration.
The page's power is at work.

00:25.300 --> 00:26.800
Which means...

00:27.550 --> 00:31.890
That I will likely be made
to be the attacker in the footage.

00:33.009 --> 00:34.929
Listen up, criminal!

00:34.929 --> 00:36.890
Drop your weapon and surrender!

00:37.479 --> 00:38.640
I repeat!

00:38.640 --> 00:41.310
I know who they are!

00:41.310 --> 00:43.520
The Five Deadly Omens...

00:43.979 --> 00:45.899
...are The Armed Detective Agency!

00:50.859 --> 00:52.530
Tanizaki, there are snipers around!

00:52.530 --> 00:54.829
Hide us with your ability.

00:54.829 --> 00:55.789
We're getting out!

00:57.250 --> 00:59.000
The snipers lost visual of the targets.

00:59.380 --> 01:00.829
It's an illusion ability.

01:00.829 --> 01:02.579
But it can't hide their body temperature.

01:03.079 --> 01:05.750
All units are to use thermal goggles.

01:05.750 --> 01:09.549
Note that bullets are useless against
the super strength and healing ability users.

01:09.549 --> 01:12.760
The assault team must be equipped
with knockout gas bolts.

01:12.760 --> 01:15.010
What're the chances
that our comms are tapped?

01:15.010 --> 01:17.269
Our transmissions
are under military encryption.

01:17.269 --> 01:17.810
Good.

01:18.060 --> 01:20.730
Those murderous wolves in sheep's clothing.

01:21.060 --> 01:22.980
Time for them to pay.

01:23.730 --> 01:25.819
Kunikida-san, over here!

01:26.439 --> 01:29.650
Those snipers must be with
the military police's anti-terrorism unit.

01:29.939 --> 01:32.909
If so the entire building
must be surrounded.

01:32.909 --> 01:35.870
Let's hand ourselves in.
We're innocent.

01:35.870 --> 01:36.989
It won't work.

01:37.370 --> 01:39.620
Ranpo-san, are you okay?

01:39.620 --> 01:42.459
I'm on the run after stopping
director Taneda from bleeding out.

01:42.829 --> 01:46.790
He may be able to testify for us
when he awakens,

01:47.709 --> 01:49.459
though I wouldn't count on it.

01:49.459 --> 01:50.879
How come?

01:50.879 --> 01:53.510
Reality has been altered by that book.

01:54.299 --> 01:59.560
The director theorized that it was created
by an ability user, but I don't think so.

01:59.890 --> 02:02.730
This is more than an ability.

02:02.730 --> 02:08.400
Case in point, Mushitaro-kun's own reality
altering ability doesn't affect memories.

02:08.939 --> 02:10.900
Yet it's happening now.

02:12.449 --> 02:13.569
He's right.

02:13.569 --> 02:17.530
I can recall abducting
the hostages and killing them.

02:21.659 --> 02:23.250
That means if we're caught...

02:23.500 --> 02:26.139
The government has
a mind-reading ability user.

02:26.139 --> 02:28.639
One look at our memories
and we'll be before the noose.

02:28.639 --> 02:29.629
Don't move!

02:31.919 --> 02:32.759
Ranpo-san!

02:40.599 --> 02:43.729
No way... they got Ranpo-san...

02:44.479 --> 02:49.770
This is what he meant when he said
the agency would be destroyed.

03:13.340 --> 03:17.840
BUNGO STRAY DOGS

04:20.490 --> 04:23.990
This is Team A. We're in front of
the room the perps are holed in.

04:24.509 --> 04:27.410
This is Team B. We've arrived
at the designated spot.

04:27.410 --> 04:28.959
Understood. Proceed.

04:35.420 --> 04:36.589
Knockout gas!

04:38.129 --> 04:39.839
Gas administered.

04:39.839 --> 04:42.139
One whiff of that
and they'll be out in seconds.

04:42.680 --> 04:45.310
Play it safe before going in
by using a cardiac sound sensor

04:45.310 --> 04:46.970
to confirm their heartbeats.

04:47.930 --> 04:51.019
HQ! We detect a faint
heartbeat from one target

04:51.019 --> 04:53.060
while the other four are unaccounted for!

04:53.060 --> 04:53.980
What?!

04:53.980 --> 04:55.019
Moving in!

05:00.199 --> 05:00.990
HQ...

05:01.699 --> 05:03.160
They're dead.

05:03.160 --> 05:04.079
Shit!

05:04.410 --> 05:05.490
Did they off themselves?

05:06.040 --> 05:08.120
Get to reviving the one with the pulse!

05:08.660 --> 05:10.689
We need them to cough out the whole story.

05:11.250 --> 05:12.959
Captain!

05:12.959 --> 05:13.850
What happened?

05:15.250 --> 05:16.670
Welcome...

05:16.670 --> 05:19.550
Impossible, she should be out like a light.

05:19.550 --> 05:23.550
Did she bleed herself to lower her blood
pressure and slow down the gas' effects?

05:24.009 --> 05:25.350
Have you heard?

05:25.350 --> 05:29.769
Humans are still briefly alive for roughly
two minutes after their heart stops.

05:29.769 --> 05:32.399
As far as the Agency's concerned,
that's as good as being unharmed!

05:32.689 --> 05:33.730
Ability!

05:33.730 --> 05:36.019
Thou Shalt Not Die!

05:42.449 --> 05:44.029
Assault team! Report back!

05:44.319 --> 05:45.579
Answer me!

05:46.079 --> 05:48.370
The assault team has ceased activity.

05:48.370 --> 05:51.040
It's likely they've all been taken out.

05:53.750 --> 05:57.170
You briefly died just to avoid
breathing in the gas?

05:57.170 --> 06:01.300
That wouldn't have been possible
without knowing when we'd strike...

06:01.300 --> 06:02.470
How was it possible?

06:02.470 --> 06:06.139
I can recreate anything
I've seen with my notebook.

06:06.529 --> 06:11.889
And I'm familiar with your encryption
from the times we've worked together.

06:13.189 --> 06:14.600
Use this to call for help.

06:14.939 --> 06:17.319
You should be fine with swift treatment.

06:19.149 --> 06:22.069
Calling all teams.
Take off your masks.

06:22.490 --> 06:24.160
If we can't rely on our comms,

06:24.160 --> 06:26.240
you'll have to move
at your own discretion.

06:26.240 --> 06:27.699
Lieutenant, where are you headed?

06:27.699 --> 06:29.120
I'm joining the front line too.

06:29.699 --> 06:32.959
I can't let any more innocents
lose their lives.

06:32.959 --> 06:34.040
Lieutenant!

06:34.040 --> 06:36.879
A large warhead is approaching us!

06:36.879 --> 06:37.500
What?!

06:37.500 --> 06:39.459
Are they coming straight for us?!

07:02.860 --> 07:07.740
This capsule does wonders
to loosen those shoulders.

07:11.870 --> 07:14.160
No need to be so stiff!

07:14.160 --> 07:15.579
Who's in charge?

07:15.579 --> 07:17.670
Hands in the air and on your knees!

07:17.670 --> 07:19.290
Are you with the Agency?

07:19.290 --> 07:23.459
Crashing at that speed would
pulverize any regular person inside!

07:24.129 --> 07:27.110
You're right,
it's a terrible mode of transport.

07:27.110 --> 07:29.009
There's no room
to even scratch your butt.

07:29.759 --> 07:30.720
Please wait.

07:31.600 --> 07:32.889
When did he appear?!

07:33.389 --> 07:37.439
Captain, you didn't bother to arrange
for a proper landing again.

07:37.439 --> 07:40.149
I was sure I fired...

07:40.480 --> 07:43.230
Jono, you're already here.

07:43.230 --> 07:45.240
Must I keep repeating myself?

07:46.899 --> 07:50.240
Please stop needlessly raising
the heartbeats of the ground forces.

07:51.160 --> 07:54.540
Could that be the remote assault shell?

07:54.540 --> 07:57.209
Does that mean they're the legendary...

07:57.209 --> 07:58.959
Everyone, lower your guns!

08:00.290 --> 08:02.209
They are reinforcements.

08:02.209 --> 08:06.589
The military police's greatest special force,
the Bloodhounds.

08:07.170 --> 08:08.470
Here come the others.

08:24.019 --> 08:25.189
I'm out.

08:25.189 --> 08:27.529
Hey, I'm stuck!

08:27.529 --> 08:29.990
Bloodshed! I demand bloodshed!

08:29.990 --> 08:33.159
Give me blood drenched sinners
begging for their sorry lives!

08:33.159 --> 08:34.730
Make it quick or I'll settle with...

08:34.730 --> 08:37.500
- Our dear fiend is in a foul mood.
- ...tearing off your limbs!

08:37.500 --> 08:39.210
Enough with the jokes, Captain.

08:39.210 --> 08:43.000
If the Vice Captain loses it here,
we'll all die.

08:44.039 --> 08:48.049
How do you open this? Let me out!

08:54.429 --> 08:56.929
You live to see another day, lackeys!

08:57.309 --> 09:03.440
Any second later and I would have pruned
your limbs and styled you into lovely bonsais.

09:03.440 --> 09:05.149
LITTLE GIRL?
A little girl?

09:05.149 --> 09:08.490
I see you're rabid as ever, Teruko-kun.

09:08.490 --> 09:10.320
I have high hopes for you.

09:10.320 --> 09:12.029
Yes, Captain!

09:12.029 --> 09:15.789
Sweet Teruko has every intention
to devote herself to being your loyal dog.

09:16.190 --> 09:18.370
These are the Bloodhounds?

09:18.370 --> 09:24.000
Indeed, those five are the cream of the crop
among the nation's military units.

09:24.389 --> 09:27.629
The Special Subjugation
Operations Group, Elite Squad.

09:28.460 --> 09:32.179
OCHI FUKUCHI
The living legend who governs them,

09:32.179 --> 09:33.929
ABILITY: LION DANCE
Ochi Fukuchi.

09:33.929 --> 09:35.639
SAIGIKU JONO
The king of ignorance

09:35.639 --> 09:37.850
whose heightened senses
comprehend everything,

09:37.850 --> 09:39.639
ABILITY: WEIGHT IN TEARS
Jono Saigiku.

09:40.320 --> 09:42.879
TETCHO SUEHIRO
Their strongest in terms of pure strength,

09:42.879 --> 09:44.610
ABILITY: PLUM BLOSSOMS IN SNOW
Tetcho Suehiro.

09:45.450 --> 09:46.379
TERUKO OKURA
The queen of bloody thorns,

09:46.379 --> 09:49.190
feared by allies and even more
by her enemies,

09:49.190 --> 09:51.070
ABILITY: SOUL'S GASP
Teruko Okura.

09:51.070 --> 09:53.659
But there are only four here...

09:54.159 --> 09:55.779
Where's the fifth?

09:55.779 --> 09:57.789
No one knows about the fifth.

09:58.240 --> 10:01.000
He's infiltrating a certain organization.

10:01.340 --> 10:03.289
I take you are the operation commander?

10:03.289 --> 10:04.210
Yes, sir!

10:04.629 --> 10:07.169
It's a pleasure to be
at your service, Fukuchi-dono.

10:07.169 --> 10:09.919
Leave the rest to us and enjoy a spot of tea.

10:10.710 --> 10:13.049
These immoral villains will be torn into

10:13.379 --> 10:15.509
by the fangs of the Bloodhounds.

10:15.509 --> 10:18.509
DOGS HUNT DOGS

10:19.139 --> 10:20.850
Please do.

10:21.679 --> 10:23.190
We'll leave it at that.

10:28.399 --> 10:31.320
Raise your hands, Fukuzawa!
You're under arrest!

10:31.899 --> 10:33.649
Damned terrorist!

10:33.649 --> 10:36.450
The Armed Detective Agency is finished.

10:40.620 --> 10:42.330
Think we got far enough?

10:44.940 --> 10:48.250
- I'm not getting any reception.
- They must be interfering with the signal.

10:48.710 --> 10:50.590
Next will be physical interferences.

10:50.919 --> 10:54.840
Observation satellites, tracking dogs,
road blocks and military drones.

10:55.129 --> 10:58.429
Our abilities will not last against those.

10:58.429 --> 11:00.509
In this modern age, having enough

11:00.509 --> 11:04.639
organized personnel and state
of the art weaponry triumphs above all.

11:05.809 --> 11:06.809
Damn it!

11:06.809 --> 11:10.980
I can't be stuck here when Naomi
could be branded a criminal!

11:12.029 --> 11:14.450
Criminal, huh...

11:18.620 --> 11:19.659
Everyone!

11:20.200 --> 11:22.159
This is the ten year orchard!

11:22.450 --> 11:26.539
In my village, an orchard
we raised for a decade

11:26.539 --> 11:30.129
was completely wiped out
by a storm overnight.

11:30.539 --> 11:33.129
We never got to harvest a single fruit.

11:33.129 --> 11:35.340
That was unfortunate.

11:35.340 --> 11:37.129
How did you think we reacted?

11:38.090 --> 11:41.889
At first we were stunned,
but then we had a little laugh

11:41.889 --> 11:43.850
and started replanting the saplings.

11:44.429 --> 11:47.690
All in order to redo that lost decade.

11:49.059 --> 11:52.190
The Agency has been met
by a terrible storm.

11:52.190 --> 11:53.649
But that's okay.

11:54.320 --> 11:59.110
Even a raging tempest brings with it
some much needed rain.

11:59.450 --> 12:02.700
Let's survive through this storm.

12:03.200 --> 12:09.879
All we can do is continue living
on this rotating rock we call the Earth.

12:11.840 --> 12:13.629
Kenji's right.

12:14.379 --> 12:17.549
We'll weather this storm
and rebuild the Agency.

12:17.799 --> 12:21.509
To do that, we must first
make a clean getaway.

12:23.639 --> 12:26.850
The more time passes,
the more resources they'll have,

12:26.850 --> 12:28.389
which widens their search area.

12:28.809 --> 12:33.110
From my experience, it'll expand
at a rate of 50 km every hour.

12:33.110 --> 12:37.490
So you're saying we have to be escaping
faster than 50 km per hour?

12:37.779 --> 12:40.200
Yeah, which is why we need transport.

12:40.200 --> 12:44.950
Meaning they have two options.
The first is the south highway.

12:44.950 --> 12:47.120
They'll steal a vehicle here and escape.

12:47.409 --> 12:49.500
The second is the train station to the north.

12:49.500 --> 12:52.330
By blending among the passengers,
they can escape via train.

12:52.330 --> 12:55.049
What excellent troops I have.

12:55.049 --> 12:59.299
I could be back at the base letting out
a loud fart and the case would be closed.

12:59.299 --> 13:01.549
That's a vulgar and unpleasant analogy.

13:01.549 --> 13:06.100
North or south, train or car.
They have two deaths to choose.

13:06.100 --> 13:11.019
Which path will these
now stray dogs turn to?

13:11.519 --> 13:12.600
We'll take a car!

13:12.600 --> 13:14.980
Why a car not the train?

13:14.980 --> 13:18.070
If they confront us
on the train and we fight,

13:18.070 --> 13:20.990
the train could derail and cause
a huge accident in town.

13:21.320 --> 13:24.700
Many innocents will lose their lives
and I won't stand for it!

13:24.700 --> 13:26.330
Which is why we go by car!

13:29.250 --> 13:30.580
That's good.

13:31.120 --> 13:33.789
This is how it should be, Kunikida.

13:37.000 --> 13:40.009
EPISODE 44:
BUNGO STRAY DOGS

13:40.879 --> 13:45.220
Now then, the station or highway?
Where do we go?

13:45.220 --> 13:46.470
Both ways.

13:46.470 --> 13:49.519
We'll take whatever they have
to throw at us and crush them.

13:49.519 --> 13:51.480
That has always been how we roll.

13:51.820 --> 13:55.230
Alrighty, me and Teruko-kun
will take the northern station.

13:55.230 --> 13:57.480
Jono and Tetcho,
you take the southern highway.

13:57.480 --> 13:59.070
Don't let them get away.

13:59.070 --> 14:02.490
Fukuchi-dono, as it happens our transport
vehicles were destroyed by the enemy,

14:02.490 --> 14:05.320
leaving us with only one
working set of wheels.

14:05.320 --> 14:06.370
No problem.

14:07.580 --> 14:10.120
Punishment awaits us if we fail.

14:10.120 --> 14:12.460
What was it again?

14:14.460 --> 14:17.710
I forgot since we never once failed.

14:17.710 --> 14:18.799
See you later.

14:34.600 --> 14:36.309
Can I help you?

14:36.309 --> 14:38.519
Does your car insurance cover theft?

14:38.519 --> 14:40.899
Yes, it does. Why?

14:40.899 --> 14:42.740
Then congratulations.

14:43.779 --> 14:45.740
You can buy yourself a new one.

14:54.210 --> 14:55.169
We're here.

14:56.750 --> 14:57.840
Tetcho-san.

14:58.419 --> 15:01.840
Was there any purpose to cutting down
the trees instead of avoiding them?

15:02.340 --> 15:05.299
Moving straight was
the shortest way to our destination.

15:05.299 --> 15:08.889
- You think like an idiot!
- How about a bite before engaging the enemy?

15:09.299 --> 15:14.100
Just so you know,
I hate you the most in this force.

15:14.100 --> 15:15.519
Hate? Why?

15:15.519 --> 15:17.860
Because your soul is bankrupt
of any artistic taste.

15:18.649 --> 15:21.899
You claimed that same
colored foods go well together

15:21.899 --> 15:24.240
and put shichimi on strawberries.

15:24.240 --> 15:26.029
Sugar on rice.

15:26.029 --> 15:27.820
Noodle sauce on red bean jelly.

15:27.820 --> 15:30.159
Now you're eating
hard boiled eggs with the shell.

15:30.159 --> 15:31.539
I wish you'd drop dead!

15:31.990 --> 15:34.580
You're useless until the enemy shows.

15:34.580 --> 15:36.789
Shut your mouth and keep quiet.

15:37.500 --> 15:41.669
Your breathing and heartbeat's
a nuisance too so silence those too.

15:41.669 --> 15:44.419
HE HELD HIS BREATH

15:48.299 --> 15:49.340
Got them.

15:49.340 --> 15:52.600
500 from here.
Four to five passengers.

15:53.470 --> 15:55.480
Heading west.

15:58.559 --> 16:00.019
Just a little more...

16:03.690 --> 16:05.940
What happened to everyone?

16:07.649 --> 16:09.950
Watch out for possible traps!

16:09.950 --> 16:11.529
The military police?

16:11.529 --> 16:13.450
They must be here to rescue the hostages!

16:13.450 --> 16:17.460
Over here! Please help me!

16:17.460 --> 16:20.039
HQ, we found one of the culprits.

16:21.059 --> 16:22.340
Requesting permission to fire!

16:25.549 --> 16:27.299
What do we do next?

16:27.299 --> 16:29.549
We lay low and gather intel.

16:30.009 --> 16:34.220
Assuming anyone will willingly shelter
a group of criminals.

16:34.679 --> 16:38.750
I know of a place
that can guarantee our safety.

16:38.750 --> 16:40.309
I'd rather not got there though.

16:40.309 --> 16:41.730
Really?

16:41.730 --> 16:42.809
Where is it?

16:42.809 --> 16:44.070
I'd love to know.

16:44.899 --> 16:48.279
Please, do tell.

16:49.860 --> 16:51.529
You're one person short.

16:51.529 --> 16:53.580
Where is the girl in the kimono?

16:53.580 --> 16:54.330
What?!

16:56.409 --> 16:58.120
He withstood Kenji's super strength?

17:00.080 --> 17:00.919
You asshole!

17:01.080 --> 17:02.289
Fine Snow!

17:08.130 --> 17:10.839
Kunikida-san, go on ahead!

17:13.470 --> 17:15.470
Well done.

17:15.470 --> 17:18.559
To think you'd erase the car,
throw my senses off

17:18.559 --> 17:20.640
and drag me out of the car.

17:20.640 --> 17:23.690
Sorry to say
but illusions don't work on me.

17:23.690 --> 17:25.400
I let you do it on purpose.

17:25.690 --> 17:28.359
We will end your lives.

17:28.359 --> 17:30.359
I just have to cut them down?

17:30.359 --> 17:33.160
Yes. Do make yourself useful,

17:33.160 --> 17:35.660
Mr. Strongest Swordsman
of the Bloodhounds.

17:36.029 --> 17:37.119
Here I come.

17:47.089 --> 17:49.720
I swear upon my ideals
that nobody gets left behind!

17:51.470 --> 17:52.930
Ready to fire!

17:53.220 --> 17:54.140
Wait!

18:14.160 --> 18:15.319
Kyoka-chan?

18:15.319 --> 18:17.529
Don't worry,
I only knocked them out.

18:20.329 --> 18:24.039
We were framed by the enemy
and the Agency was labeled as criminals.

18:24.039 --> 18:26.000
Everyone's fled from here.

18:26.630 --> 18:27.339
Come on.

18:27.339 --> 18:28.589
Where are we going?

18:28.589 --> 18:30.130
We have to get away too.

18:30.509 --> 18:32.220
There's no escape now.

18:32.720 --> 18:34.970
We have no way out.

18:34.970 --> 18:36.220
Kenji!

18:36.509 --> 18:38.720
There's no time to stop! Hang on!

18:46.230 --> 18:47.900
Oh dear.

18:47.900 --> 18:49.819
This is the worst!

18:49.819 --> 18:53.069
That's the military police's
greatest special force, the Bloodhounds!

18:53.069 --> 18:55.910
They had body enhancements
by special ability technicians,

18:55.910 --> 18:58.410
granting them physical capabilities
far beyond average.

18:59.410 --> 19:03.160
If they catch up again, the car will be
destroyed along with our chances of escaping!

19:03.789 --> 19:07.329
You've been extremely
useless today, Tetcho-san.

19:07.329 --> 19:09.289
Have you considered a new job?

19:09.289 --> 19:11.759
Alright, I've warmed up.

19:12.049 --> 19:14.839
Oh, he's a little mad
from being run over.

19:15.509 --> 19:17.640
There is evil that goes punished.

19:18.140 --> 19:20.220
There is good that goes unrewarded.

19:20.509 --> 19:22.470
Without this blade of mine,

19:22.930 --> 19:26.519
how does all that is good
and bad in the world

19:26.519 --> 19:28.980
ever hope to achieve equilibrium?

19:31.019 --> 19:32.900
Plum Blossoms in Snow!

19:50.710 --> 19:52.130
What did they do?

19:52.130 --> 19:55.130
Turning back to rescue your allies
instead of abandoning them,

19:55.130 --> 19:57.799
but alas, it leads to all your deaths.

19:57.799 --> 20:00.390
A pretty typical turn of events.

20:01.259 --> 20:02.059
Look out!

20:07.640 --> 20:09.769
None shall escape my blade.

20:10.440 --> 20:12.650
I still can't tell what attack that is.

20:13.359 --> 20:14.690
As things stand...

20:14.690 --> 20:16.109
Doppo Poetry!

20:16.109 --> 20:16.779
Stun gre...

20:22.369 --> 20:25.000
I saw the moment he drew his sword.

20:25.579 --> 20:28.500
It extended far beyond
the length of the scabbard

20:29.210 --> 20:30.539
and could even bend.

20:35.920 --> 20:40.009
Furthermore, it could travel
far enough to slice a speeding car.

20:40.299 --> 20:43.180
Which means we'll never outrun that blade.

20:44.009 --> 20:48.480
We're completely outmatched
by the Bloodhounds...

20:48.769 --> 20:50.559
Now then, Tetcho-san.

20:50.559 --> 20:53.440
Start by beheading the good doctor.

20:55.150 --> 20:57.900
We can't have her healing her allies.

20:57.900 --> 21:00.859
Not to mention she is the angel of death.

21:00.859 --> 21:03.119
Your demise will benefit the world.

21:03.410 --> 21:05.240
Stop, don't kill her!

21:05.240 --> 21:07.200
Fine, we surrender!

21:07.200 --> 21:09.500
What a fascinating heartbeat.

21:09.960 --> 21:12.750
Kunikida-san the idealist,

21:12.750 --> 21:15.630
you were relieved just now, no?

21:16.130 --> 21:17.420
What?

21:17.420 --> 21:19.220
I've read the reports.

21:19.759 --> 21:24.009
Your ideals are as grand as
and soar high like a blimp.

21:24.009 --> 21:29.230
But a blimp will one day
run out of fuel and be forced to land.

21:29.230 --> 21:32.400
You live in fear of that day.

21:32.400 --> 21:33.309
Don't do it...

21:33.309 --> 21:35.609
I congratulate you, Kunikida-san.

21:35.609 --> 21:37.980
You'll be free
from that fear from tomorrow!

21:43.990 --> 21:47.369
Charge, gravity manipulation.

21:51.920 --> 21:54.039
A supersonic shot?

21:54.039 --> 21:55.839
But I didn't hear anything being fired!

21:58.210 --> 22:00.130
I see the Agency's still up to dumb shit!

22:03.839 --> 22:07.059
The Boss asked me to come pick you up!

23:35.809 --> 23:37.730
BUNGO STRAY DOGS

23:37.730 --> 23:40.019
EPISODE 45:
WE ARE BOTH SINNERS
